{#
Generated by: Claude Code CLI
Date time: 2026/08/21 10:32 SAST
Version: 0.5.7.6
Description:
  Bounded entity picker replacing the whole-table dropdown controls on Activity, Credits and
  the person profile.

  Caller sets:
    lk_name      hidden field name submitted with the form, e.g. "company_id"
    lk_type      lookup type: people, companies, courses or assignable_courses
    lk_base      which lookup endpoint to search, defaulting to the Administration one. The Company
                 workspace has its own, guarded by company permissions and scoped to the company
                 being administered, because the Administration lookup is guarded by platform
                 permissions a company administrator does not hold and must not be given.
    lk_label     visible label
    lk_selected  the currently selected entity, carrying id, label and detail, or null
    lk_required  optional "1" to require a selection
    lk_empty     optional label for the "no selection" state

  Progressive enhancement: without htmx the hidden field still holds the current value and
  the form still submits correctly; the search box simply does nothing. The control never
  becomes the only way to keep an already-chosen value.

Changelog:
  2026/08/21 11:04 SAST
  - Rewrote every comment in this file in plain prose. Comments must never carry angle brackets, comment delimiters, template tokens or code: a comment delimiter written inside a comment ends it early and leaks the remainder onto the page.
  2026/08/21 10:32 SAST
  - Moved the guard note out of the hidden input start tag. A comment opened inside a start tag is not treated as a comment: the browser reads it as attribute text and ends the element early, so the value and required attributes were emitted as page text and the field submitted an empty id, silently discarding an already-selected person, company or course.
  2026/08/21 01:00 SAST
  - Guarded the selection before dereferencing it; the falsy "nothing selected" default cannot take a property access.
  2026/08/20 20:02 SAST
  - Created for the v0.5.7.6 pagination and large-data UI foundations release.
#}
<div class="field full entity-lookup" data-entity-lookup="{{ lk_name }}">

  <label for="{{ lk_name }}-search">{{ lk_label }}</label>

  {# Keep this note outside the tag below. A comment opened inside a start tag is not treated
       as a comment: the browser reads it as attribute text and ends the element early, which
       silently drops every attribute written after it. The value expression below guards the
       selection before reading its id, because the "nothing selected" default is a falsy
       scalar and cannot be dereferenced. #}
  <input type="hidden"
         id="{{ lk_name }}-value"
         name="{{ lk_name }}"
         value="{{ lk_selected ? lk_selected.id : '' }}"
         {{ lk_required ? 'required' : '' }}>

  <p class="lookup-selected" id="{{ lk_name }}-selected" aria-live="polite">
    {% if lk_selected %}
      <strong>{{ lk_selected.label }}</strong> <span class="muted">{{ lk_selected.detail }}</span>{% else %}<span class="muted">{{ lk_empty ?: 'Nothing selected' }}</span>
    {% endif %}
  </p>

  <input type="search"
         id="{{ lk_name }}-search"
         class="lookup-search"
         placeholder="Search {{ lk_type }}…"
         autocomplete="off"
         maxlength="120"
         aria-controls="{{ lk_name }}-results"
         hx-get="{{ lk_base is defined and lk_base ? lk_base : '/admin/lookup' }}/{{ lk_type }}"
         hx-trigger="keyup changed delay:250ms, search"
         hx-target="#{{ lk_name }}-results"
         hx-vals='{"target": "{{ lk_name }}"}'
         name="q">

  <div class="lookup-results-panel" id="{{ lk_name }}-results" role="region" aria-live="polite">
    <p class="help lookup-hint">Type at least 2 characters to search.</p>
  </div>

  {% if lk_selected %}
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm lookup-clear" data-lookup-clear="{{ lk_name }}">Clear selection</button>
  {% endif %}

</div>
